# Cloudflare Pages headers (https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/)

# Allow other GPSA sites to fetch the per-season scores feeds cross-origin.
# These are static public JSON files; a plain GET is a CORS "simple request"
# (no preflight), so this single response header is the entire CORS surface.
#
# There are now two consumers — the meet-schedule site, and the Rules Committee
# portal dashboard at submit.gpsaswimming.org. `_headers` takes one static value
# per header and cannot reflect an origin, so two named origins is not
# expressible; `*` is the only mechanism that serves both.
#
# It grants nothing new. These files are already served unauthenticated to any
# client that asks — plain curl gets a 200 — so `*` widens only what *browser
# JavaScript on another origin* may read, not who may read it. If that ever
# stops being true, the fix is to stop publishing the file, not to narrow this
# header.
/*/scores.json
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
